gAm(){return"How your plan works"},
gAl(){return"A plan that adjusts to you, not the other way around."},
gAk(){return"You start from where you really are"},
gAj(){return"We ask what you can do today. The plan starts there, not from a generic number."},
gAi(){return"Progress without getting hurt"},
gAh(){return"The load grows by at most 15% a week, and every fourth week is lighter so you can recover."},
gAc(){return"It adapts to every day"},
gAb(){return"Before training you tell us how you feel. With that, your fatigue and your results, we adjust today's session and tell you why."},
gAe(){return"It learns from how it feels"},
gAd(){return"When you finish, you rate how hard it was. That tells us how much you had left and fine-tunes what comes next."},
gAa(){return"You decide the big changes"},
gA9(){return"If your real pace drifts from the plan, we suggest a new date. We never change your goal without asking."},
gAg(){return"Your data stays on your phone"},
gAf(){return"Everything is calculated and stored on your device. No accounts, no cloud."},
grJ(){return"Got it"},
gzj(){return"See how it works in detail"},
gpd(){return"How your plan works"},
gpc(){return"Back"},
gz9(){return"Road To combines a long-term plan with a daily adjustment. The plan sets the path to your goal; the daily adjustment fits each session to how you are. Everything is calculated on your phone."},
gzi(){return"What we see today"},
gze(){return"Estimated capacity"},
gzg(){return"Fatigue"},
gxB(){return"Low"},
gxC(){return"Medium"},
gxA(){return"High"},
gzd(){return"Consistency (14 days)"},
gzh(){return"Improvement per week"},
gzf(){return"Days since your last session"},
gzl(){return"1. Your plan"},
gzk(){return"It starts at what you can do today (your initial test) and rises gradually to the goal by the target date. You choose your rest days. Each training day is split into sets shaped for the exercise: warm-up sets building to the day's number, equal sets, a pyramid, or one continuous effort for running."},
gzp(){return"2. Safety limits"},
gzo(){return"The load grows by at most about 15% a week. If you pick a date that would require ramping up faster, we push it out; we never pull it in. Every fourth week drops to 60% so you can recover, except the last one, so you reach the goal at full strength. If you give us your age, height, weight or activity level, the pace may be more cautious."},
gz_(){return"3. The daily adjustment"},
gyZ(){return"Before you start, you tell us how you feel. With that and your history we adjust only today's session:"},
gz4(){return"Mood: exhausted \u221220%, low \u221210%, energized +5%."},
gz1(){return"Coming back after 5, 10 or 21+ days off: \u221210%, \u221220% or \u221230%."},
gz3(){return"Accumulated fatigue: \u22128% or \u221215%."},
gz2(){return"If your recent results are clearly below the plan, we come down to your level; if they're clearly above and you're rested, we go up by as much as 10%."},
gz0(){return"The adjustment never goes beyond \u221235% or +10%, never goes up during a lighter week, and when signals conflict, recovery wins. We always show you why, and you can do the original plan with one tap."},
gzc(){return"4. How it learns from you"},
gza(){return"Your capacity isn't just what you did, but how hard it was: 30 reps rated very easy means you had more in you; 30 rated very hard means you were at your limit. Recent sessions count more than older ones, and after more than 5 days off the estimate drops a little."},
gzb(){return"Fatigue combines the sessions you rated hard, time spent paused, and whether this week you did much more than your monthly average, a well-known injury-risk signal. We also track your consistency, your pace (for running), your real weekly improvement and your weight."},
gyY(){return"5. When the plan changes"},
gyX(){return"The overall plan only changes if you accept it. We suggest it when you miss a training day, when what you did is more than 20% off what was asked that day, or when two of your last three sessions felt clearly easier or harder than expected. A single bad day doesn't move your date. You can keep your pace or pick the fastest one that's still safe."},
gz8(){return"6. Summary and recommendations"},
gz7(){return"After each session we show how you did against the target, whether it was a personal best, how your estimated capacity changed, and your next session. In Progress you'll find recommendations: an extra rest day, managing load, your real pace against the plan's date, and more."},
gzr(){return"7. Automatic tracking"},
gzq(){return"If your exercise supports it, the phone counts reps, times your hold, or measures distance by GPS. You can always correct it or finish manually."},
gzn(){return"8. Your data"},
gzm(){return"Everything is calculated and stored on your phone: no accounts, no cloud, no ads. If you delete the app, your data is deleted."},
gz6(){return"Important"},
gz5(){return"These rules are training guidelines, not medical advice. If you feel pain, dizziness or shortness of breath, stop. See a professional if you have an injury or a health condition."},
